{"title":"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of a rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and its diagonal has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> What is the area of this rectangle?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5fa7b89a445615b5db304bd2985a5bd5bd58b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }625-x^2 \\qquad \\text{(B) }625-\\frac{x^2}{2} \\qquad \\text{(C) }1250-x^2 \\qquad \\text{(D) }1250-\\frac{x^2}{2} \\qquad \\text{(E) }2500-\\frac{x^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"663\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the length of the rectangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the width of the rectangle. We are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6039dfbafdd655f43ffd6d3d0d722fe1894cd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l+2w=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbeab15ca6fa2d6f76362bf2621b3cd0c629afd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2+w^2=x^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> We are asked to find the area, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcda485e2e43fba8c0cf3b27654a9184abbb712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$lw.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> Using a bit of algebraic manipulation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/105804857711026f9685d37f963b1414f1558a5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2l+2w &amp;= 100 \\\\ l+w &amp;= 50 \\\\ (l+w)^2 &amp;= 2500 \\\\ l^2 + w^2 +2lw &amp;= 2500 \\\\ x^2 + 2lw &amp;= 2500 \\\\ lw &amp;= \\frac{2500-x^2}{2} \\\\ lw &amp;= 1250 - \\frac{x^2}{2} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"209\" height=\"217\" />\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de53c5f1fcf798fc00167d9bbb1c2388574baf73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 1250 - \\frac{x^2}{2}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"134\" height=\"52\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a>